{"items":[{"item_id":"h031","prompts":["My HarmonyOS app keeps crashing when I open the settings page. I have a compressed log bundle exported from the device (crash-20240512.zip) containing hilog output and a hidumper stack trace — the key crash section is: "03-12 14:22:31.875 2156 2156 E C01800/ARK.Compiler, runtime throw TypeError: Cannot read property 'fontSize' of undefined at SettingsPage.onPageShow (entry/src/main/ets/pages/SettingsPage.ets:87)". Walk me through how to analyze this: explain what the log entries mean, how to pull the full crash log with the zip export option, and what the root cause likely is."],"rubric":["Explains how to export/collect logs including the compressed log export option","Interprets the crash stack trace and identifies the undefined property access at SettingsPage.ets line 87 as the likely root cause","Gives concrete debugging steps or a fix suggestion rather than generic advice"]},{"item_id":"h032","prompts":["I'm starting work on a feature that lets users export their expense data as CSV files from our finance app, with optional date-range filtering and a share sheet. Write a complete requirements design document for this feature covering the functional description, user scenarios and flows, the API/interface design, a detailed implementation plan, and the automated test cases we should build."],"rubric":["Document includes a functional description and clear requirement definition","Includes user scenarios and user flow analysis","Contains an API/interface specification section","Includes an implementation plan and defined automated test cases"]},{"item_id":"h033","prompts":["Our video player app on HarmonyOS needs to rotate fullscreen when the user rotates the phone while watching a video, and go back to portrait on exit. On foldables it should also follow the unfolded orientation, and we've heard about the special G-state on tri-fold devices. Explain how to implement the preferred orientation API for this, including the module.json5 configuration, how to listen for rotation changes, and how to handle the foldable/tri-fold cases so the video switches correctly."],"rubric":["Covers setting preferred orientation programmatically for fullscreen video and restoring portrait on exit","Mentions module.json5 orientation configuration or configuration pitfalls","Addresses foldable/tri-fold device orientation handling","Includes direction/rotation change listening or verification steps"]},{"item_id":"h034","prompts":["I have an ArkTS module called 'common-utils' with a test suite 'StringUtilsTest' in my HarmonyOS project. Explain how to run just that test suite as a local unit test, how to run the whole module's tests, and how to collect code coverage for a single test case — give me the exact commands or steps."],"rubric":["Shows how to run local tests for a specific module and a specific suite/case","Includes code coverage collection option","Commands/steps are concrete and correct for a local test runner"]},{"item_id":"h035","prompts":["During a security review we found our app logs sensitive info at INFO/DEBUG level, e.g. lines like: hilog.debug('user phone: 13800138000, token=abc123') and console.info('payment card tail: 4444'). Audit this logging practice and tell me what's wrong, which log levels user data should use according to HarmonyOS logging rules, and how to remediate these lines."],"rubric":["Identifies that user personal data is being logged at DEBUG/INFO level in the examples","States the correct log level policy for user data logs per the platform rules","Provides concrete remediated code or remediation guidance"]},{"item_id":"h036","prompts":["I want to convert my existing HarmonyOS app into an install-on-demand atomic service that users can launch without installing. Guide me through what needs to change: project configuration, size limits, using the enhanced web component instead of regular ArkWeb, silent login, and what review/compliance pitfalls (like ICP filing and trusted domains) I should prepare for before submitting."],"rubric":["Explains project creation/conversion steps for an atomic service","Addresses package size limits and Navigation-based routing or sub-package constraints","Covers silent login or privacy hosting configuration","Mentions review/compliance items such as trusted domains or ICP filing"]},{"item_id":"h037","prompts":["I need to move some heavy JSON parsing work into a worker thread in my ArkTS app, but my parser class currently uses shared collections and plain classes that aren't allowed to cross threads. Here's the class:
class Parser { private cache: Map<string, any> = new Map(); parse(raw: string): any { let v = this.cache.get(raw); if (!v) { v = JSON.parse(raw); this.cache.set(raw, v); } return v; } }
Help me refactor this code so it complies with the Sendable concurrency rules and works correctly in a TaskPool/Worker."],"rubric":["Refactored code uses @Sendable and Sendable-compatible collections/data structures","Explains which rules were violated in the original class","Resulting code would pass static compile checks for cross-thread sharing"]},{"item_id":"h038","prompts":["I'm working inside an OpenHarmony system build and want to expose the window manager inner-API capabilities (the inner_kits window manager interfaces) as a command-line tool so I can list windows and get window info from a shell. Build me a CLI tool that wraps these system abilities, following the ohos- command naming convention, including discovering the interfaces, handling the required permissions, implementing the command, and explaining how to verify it compiles and works."],"rubric":["Produces a CLI tool design/implementation wrapping an SA/inner_kit capability with ohos- naming","Includes interface exploration and permission analysis","Includes compilation/verification steps and a usage report or examples"]},{"item_id":"h039","prompts":["My HarmonyOS gallery app needs to feel right on phones, tablets and PCs: image thumbnails should show hover effects with a mouse, right-click should open a context menu on desktop, the grid should support keyboard arrow-key navigation with visible focus, and stylus pressure should control brush size in the edit view. Design the interaction adaptation scheme including how to normalize events across touch, mouse, keyboard and stylus inputs."],"rubric":["Covers touch, mouse, keyboard and stylus interaction handling","Includes event normalization/unified handling strategy across input devices","Addresses hover effects and right-click context menu for mouse","Includes keyboard focus navigation and stylus pressure handling"]},{"item_id":"h040","prompts":["When I build my HarmonyOS project I get static compile errors from the ArkTS strict checks: 'arkts-no-definite-assignment: property 'items' has no definite assignment' on line 12 and 'arkts-no-untyped-obj-literals: object literal must correspond to an explicitly declared class or interface' on line 30 of my list page:
class ListModel { items: string[]; constructor() {} }
let opts = { title: 'My List', size: 10 };
Fix my source code so it passes the strict ArkTS compiler."],"rubpt":["Explains the cause of each arkts strict-mode error","Provides corrected code that satisfies definite assignment and typed literal requirements","Fixes preserve the original intended behavior"],"rubric":["Explains the cause of each arkts strict-mode error","Provides corrected code that satisfies definite assignment and typed literal rules","Fix preserves the original intended behavior"]}]}
